            "body": "@BBuf @HaiShaw this is an AMD-only fix: on gfx942 (MI325X) the DSA bf16 decode kernel blows past the 64 KB LDS under dp-attention (64 heads on a rank needs 115200 B), so the server won't even come up. It caps the per-block heads to 16 on gfx942 using the kernel's existing REPLICATE_H split, gated so gfx950 and the TP-sharded paths are untouched. Validated on a real MI325X (details in the description). CI is behind the run-ci label and I can't add it from my account, so a /tag-and-rerun-ci and a review pass would be great. cc @saienduri for the AMD runners.",
