  "inline_comments": [],
  "issue_comments": [
    {
      "body": "@BBuf @HaiShaw this is an AMD-only fix: on gfx942 (MI325X) the DSA bf16 decode kernel blows past the 64 KB LDS under dp-attention (64 heads on a rank needs 115200 B), so the server won't even come up. It caps the per-block heads to 16 on gfx942 using the kernel's existing REPLICATE_H split, gated so gfx950 and the TP-sharded paths are untouched. Validated on a real MI325X (details in the description). CI is behind the run-ci label and I can't add it from my account, so a /tag-and-rerun-ci and a review pass would be great. cc @saienduri for the AMD runners.",
      "created_at": "2026-08-07T17:14:29Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/34010#issuecomment-5219985105",
      "id": 5219985105,
      "updated_at": "2026-08-07T17:14:29Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "reger-men"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "@BBuf @HaiShaw this needs run-ci and I can't self-add it. Validated on real gfx942/MI325X: the stock LDS overflow crash is fixed, dp-attention captures 52/52, needle correct at 32k/131k vs TP4, and it's inert on gfx950. Could you add the label and take a codeowner pass? cc @saienduri for the AMD runners.",
      "created_at": "2026-08-13T16:01:41Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/34010#issuecomment-5283016710",
      "id": 5283016710,
      "updated_at": "2026-08-13T16:01:41Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "reger-men"
